    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n100623" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνθνῄσκω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-θᾰνοῦμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1139
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				979
			</span></i>:—<i>die with</i> or <i>together</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i> ll.cc., <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				720
			</span></i>, etc.: c. dat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θανόντι
			συνθανεῖν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				798
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				953
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of things,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνθνῄσκουσα δὲ σποδός</span>
			<i>expiring with</i> (the flames), <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				819
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ γὰρ ηὑσέβεια</span> (cj.
			for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ γὰρ εὐσέβεια</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ς. βροτοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1443
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ποίησις οὐχὶ συντέθνηκέ μοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					868
				</span></i>
			; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συναποθνῄσκω</span>.</div>
